==== OEM installation using the TFTP method ====

->  [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing.tftp]]

=== Specific values needed for tftp ===

<WRAP BOX>

^ Bootloader tftp server IPv4 address  | 192.168.1.82|
^ Firmware tftp image                  | [[:downloads|Latest OpenWrt release]] (**''NOTE:''** initramfs-like) |
^ TFTP transfer window                 | 20 seconds                                |
^ TFTP window start                    | approximately 1-2 seconds after power on   |

</WRAP>

  - download the latest nbg-419n2-initramfs-kernel.bin
  - use hexedit and change first 4 bytes to "Zyxel-like" u-boot magic number  FF A8 30 90
  - count new CRC32 of u-boot header (64 bytes) and write next 4 bytes (7A BE 7A CE for [[https://downloads.openwrt.org/releases/18.06.5/targets/ramips/rt305x/openwrt-18.06.5-ramips-rt305x-nbg-419n2-initramfs-kernel.bin|openwrt-18.06.5-ramips-rt305x-nbg-419n2-initramfs-kernel.bin]]), (DE 36 96 56 for [[https://archive.openwrt.org/releases/19.07.4/targets/ramips/rt305x/openwrt-19.07.4-ramips-rt305x-nbg-419n2-initramfs-kernel.bin|openwrt-19.07.4-ramips-rt305x-nbg-419n-initramfs-kernel.bin]]) 
  - you can count CRC32 by zeroing the 4 bytes next to the magic word (FF A8 30 90) then go to [[https://www.lammertbies.nl/comm/info/crc-calculation|online crc32 calculator]] and get the new value to replace the zeros (CRC32 checksum)
  - start tftp server  IP 192.168.1.82
  - rename changed image file to NBG419Nv2.bin and set to tftp server
  - connect any lan port with server
  - press and hold the WPS key button on device and power on 
  - after  20-30 second your openWrt on ip 192.168.1.1 is ready and waiting  

